From bb949a086090b9c448670b655cd2a3ea39090d46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:38:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] camera: A video resolution button for cameras of
 camera-hal-bridge

camera-hal-bridge offers each camera's stream in the sizes its HAL lists
for YUV output (720p, 1080p, 4K), 720p first. Aperture took the best
caps by its own rules, which leave out portrait sizes above 1080 lines
and so always took the first, 720p.

The viewfinder gets a video-size property: the shorter side of the
camera format to use, 0 for the best one as before; a change starts the
stream again with that format. In video mode, a button beside the scene
button shows the resolution (720p, 1080p, 4K) and goes on to the next
one on offer when tapped; the choice is kept in the settings
(video-resolution, 1080 by default). 4K is offered only with the
hardware encoder, which software encoding cannot keep up with. In
picture mode the stream keeps the camera's default: photos come from the
HAL at full size anyway.
